tags: [parse, syntax, declaration, top-level]
description: "Expected a valid top-level declaration or rule"
---

The parser expected a valid top-level declaration or rule (`let`, `type`, `fn`, `test`, `extern`, `use`, `set`, or `static-assert`), or a directive (`@name`) preceding a declaration, but encountered an unexpected token.

## Example

This error occurs when stray punctuation, an invalid keyword, or a directive attached to a `set` or `static-assert` rule appears at the top level:

```kura
@deprecated
set button(fill: red)

pub fn helper(): Int => 1
```

## Solution

Ensure every top-level item starts with a supported declaration keyword, and remove directives from `set` rules and `static-assert` statements:

```kura
set button(fill: red)

fn helper(): Int => 1
```
